== The Final Forty — Questions

#mcq(1, [Damage to the motor neurones would cause], [muscles to stop responding to impulses], [loss of sensation], [improved coordination], [ blindness])

#mcq(2, [Accommodation of the eye is achieved by], [changing the size of the pupil], [changing the shape of the lens], [moving the retina], [closing the eyelid])

#mcq(3, [Insulin lowers the blood glucose level by], [converting glycogen to glucose], [breaking down protein], [absorbing water], [converting glucose to glycogen])

#mcq(4, [Double fertilisation in a flowering plant refers to], [two pollen tubes entering the ovule], [two eggs being fertilised], [one male gamete fusing with the egg and the other with the polar nuclei], [two flowers being pollinated at once])

#mcq(5, [After ovulation the ruptured follicle develops into the], [placenta], [corpus luteum], [endometrium], [cervix])

#mcq(6, [A growth curve that rises in steps is characteristic of], [a human being], [a tree], [an insect], [a fish])

#mcq(7, [Memory cells are important because they], [make the second response to a pathogen faster and larger], [engulf bacteria], [produce mucus], [carry oxygen])

#mcq(8, [The carbon that leaves dead matter during decay enters the atmosphere as], [carbon monoxide], [methane only], [carbonate], [carbon dioxide])

#mcq(9, [Cocaine is dangerous because it], [is a mild sedative], [is highly addictive and damages the heart], [is used to treat malaria], [has no effect on the brain])

#mcq(10, [A control experiment is set up], [with the variable changed], [in a different laboratory], [with no measurements], [without the variable, but otherwise identical])

#mcq(11, [The myelin sheath around a neurone], [insulates the axon and speeds up the impulse], [slows the impulse], [produces neurotransmitters], [contains the nucleus])

#mcq(12, [The vitreous humour], [is a bone], [moves the eye], [is a jelly filling the eyeball behind the lens], [produces tears])

#mcq(13, [Cortisol, which helps the body resist long-term stress, is secreted by the], [adrenal medulla], [pituitary], [thyroid], [adrenal cortex])

#mcq(14, [The stalk that carries the anther is the], [style], [filament], [pedicel], [receptacle])

#mcq(15, [The LH surge causes], [the lining to thicken], [menstruation], [ovulation], [the placenta to form])

#mcq(16, [Growth in plants is described as 'unlimited' because], [meristems keep dividing throughout the life of the plant], [plants grow only when young], [plants never stop making seeds], [plants grow only in the dark])

#mcq(17, [The causative organism of cholera is], [Vibrio cholerae, a bacterium], [a virus], [Plasmodium], [a fungus])

#mcq(18, [Freezing preserves food because], [it kills all micro-organisms], [it removes water], [it adds salt], [low temperature stops growth and enzyme action])

#mcq(19, [A tourniquet should be used only when], [there is a small cut], [the casualty has a headache], [bleeding cannot be controlled by pressure and the limb would otherwise be lost], [the casualty is unconscious])

#mcq(20, [Which of these is a valid conclusion from an experiment?], [The result agrees with my guess], [Within the range tested, increasing light intensity increased the rate of bubbling], [Photosynthesis is important], [The plant is green])

#mcq(21, [The hypothalamus is important because it], [stores memories], [produces bile], [controls body temperature, hunger, thirst and the pituitary], [filters the blood])

#mcq(22, [The sense of smell is detected by], [taste buds], [olfactory cells in the nasal lining], [hair cells in the ear], [rods in the eye])

#mcq(23, [The main symptoms of untreated diabetes mellitus include], [excessive thirst, frequent urination and glucose in the urine], [weight gain and slow heartbeat], [goitre and bulging eyes], [night blindness])

#mcq(24, [Grafting involves joining], [two seeds], [two flowers], [two roots], [the scion of one plant to the stock of another])

#mcq(25, [Fertilisation in a human being normally takes place in the], [uterus], [ovary], [oviduct], [cervix])

#mcq(26, [A graph of height against age for a human being has a flattened top because], [the person stops eating], [the measurements are wrong], [height decreases with age], [growth has stopped in adulthood])

#mcq(27, [Which of these is a fungal disease?], [Athlete's foot], [Typhoid], [Malaria], [Polio])

#mcq(28, [Viruses can reproduce only], [in soil], [inside a living host cell], [in water], [in dead matter])

#mcq(29, [Refuse collection is a public-health measure because], [it removes breeding sites for flies and rats], [it makes the town look tidy], [it provides fertiliser], [it reduces noise])

#mcq(30, [When drawing a graph from experimental data, the independent variable is usually plotted], [on the y-axis], [in the title], [on the x-axis], [in the key])

#mcq(31, [The spinal cord is protected by the], [cranium], [vertebral column], [ribs], [pelvis])

#mcq(32, [The skin detects all of the following except], [pressure], [temperature], [pain], [light])

#mcq(33, [ADH (antidiuretic hormone) acts on the], [liver], [heart], [lungs], [kidney tubules])

#mcq(34, [The endosperm of a seed is important because it], [protects the seed], [attracts insects], [provides food for the developing embryo], [helps dispersal])

#mcq(35, [The epididymis is important because it], [produces testosterone], [stores sperm while they mature], [adds fluid to the semen], [carries urine])

#mcq(36, [The part of a plant in which growth occurs by cell division is the], [meristem], [xylem], [leaf blade], [root hair])

#mcq(37, [Which of these is a deficiency disease?], [Malaria], [Rickets], [Tuberculosis], [Cholera])

#mcq(38, [Biogas is mainly], [carbon dioxide], [oxygen], [hydrogen], [methane])

#mcq(39, [Hypovolaemic shock results from], [a serious loss of blood or fluid], [too much blood], [a broken bone], [a burn only])

#mcq(40, [In capture–recapture, the estimate is calculated from], [the number marked and the number in the first sample], [the size of the site only], [the number marked, the size of the second sample and the number of marked animals in it], [the weight of the animals])

